<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n60660" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κύκλ-ωμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>,
			τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>that which is rounded into a circle</i>: </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<i>wheel</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. Ἰξίονος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Ph.</u>
					[1185]
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βυρσότονον κ.</span>
			<i>drum</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ba.</u>
				124
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>coil</i> of a serpent, <i><span class="en">
				D.S.
				3.36
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>4.</b> of natural
			objects, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἰθέριον κ.</span>, of the sun,
				<i><span class="en">
				Secund.
				<u>Sent.</u>
				5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κόσμος ἀπλανὲς κ.</span>
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
